	'M3-F8':
		"`probe.capture()` again on request, with the moved object's reflection settling: `crates/null3d-render/tests/probes.rs`, the `probe-capture` picture on every tier, and the `probe-blend` picture on every tier; `docs/api/scene.md`. The `probe-blend` references on WebGPU and compatibility mode were drawn on 21 October, before this branch, and held the east half without its probe; M3-R36 fixed that fault and redrew them from this Mac and from CI. The compatibility-mode picture had failed three full runs against a reference drawn on a slow run; the page now pins the frame-budget governor (d3dda9e72), and the full run on 57a0a08ed passed that picture on every tier. A capture on request could still be lost three ways. The frame loop could skip the capture's frame whole, and the hold loop skipped the held frame that captures when the next held frame changed the plan; `packages/engine/src/render/loop.test.ts` holds that both draw. The pipeline guard then kept a probe's request in a held frame that had drawn no frame, so the first probe captured twice and the second never captured; `crates/null3d-render/tests/probes.rs` captures two probes across the held frames on both builders, from the round 26 checker's reproduction, and the guard's unit test in `crates/null3d-render/src/probes.rs` ends the request before any frame is drawn and keeps it while a later frame's pipelines build. A pick in flight across a GPU loss rejects with E1436 and is not asked again, which M3-R35 closed. The page reports the frames it skipped (D-206). Full run 40405229465 at `6abef3495` passed `probe-blend` on webgpu in 5.5 s, compat in 5.9 s and webgl2 in 3.8 s, and `probe-capture` on webgpu in 18.8 s, compat in 19.3 s and webgl2 in 12.3 s (shard 10, job 121862656898). On the Mac at `faf5fcd60` the held probe pictures passed 12 of 12, `probe-capture` 48 of 48 on the GPU and 48 of 48 on SwiftShader, and the TAA captures 5 of 5. The two-probe Rust test fails with `[0, 0]` without the guard's fix.",
	'M3-E2':
		"The hook carries the add-on's selection, nearest first, and the engine's transparent pass sorts the chosen rows: `tests/image/addon-tasks.spec.ts` proves a task runs on a job worker, and the `--splats` case of `bun run bench:allocation` passed at `dc1e9d557` on the Mac's WebGL2 (506.7 bytes a frame on the sketch worker, 138.3 on the render worker) and on the software renderer (1,159.7 and 534.6), with every place inside its budget; `.dev/benchmarks.md`'s `--splats` bullet records the run; the owner's ruling of 26 October 2026 keeps this line, and D-173's addendum gives the reasons",
